# Website relation (explorations vs MCP)

## One capability, three presentations

| Layer | Role |
| --- | --- |
| Website exploration | Human textbook — pedagogy, widgets, curated examples |
| MCP docs `use/eips/eip-NNNN` | Human inspiration — same problem set, prompts, Connect |
| Engine module + generic tools | Runtime — execute **caller-supplied** bytecode |

## Canonical source of truth

- **Schema:** `website/src/explorations/canonicalTypes.ts`
- **Instance:** `website/src/explorations/eip-NNNN/canonical.ts` → `CANONICAL`
- Replicate into engine `EipCapability` and mcp-docs prose. **Website wins** on conflict.
- Do **not** import from `website/src/explorations/` into this repo.

## Twin, not clone — no orphan explorations

- Same **core question** — different **artifact**
- Exploration is a **slice**; MCP is a **superset**
- Every **live** exploration needs an MCP-docs EIP page (Runnable or Planned)
- Website owns **interactive examples**; MCP owns **general execution**
- Do **not** replay exploration widget bytecode in the engine catalog

## Adding exploration does not auto-add MCP module

Website `add-exploration` skill is out of scope for engine work unless requested. A new exploration without a runnable module still needs `mcp-docs/use/eips/eip-NNNN.md`. Module work: [add-mcp-module skill](../skills/add-mcp-module/SKILL.md).

## Cross-links (human docs only)

- Exploration → MCP docs: `/use/eips/eip-NNNN` (when page exists)
- MCP docs → exploration: feelyourprotocol.org route + EIP spec
